# FDF UI/UX Quality Standards

## Mandatory Skills

**When creating or substantially redesigning an interface**, read and follow:
`.agents/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md`

**When reviewing or validating UI quality**, read and follow:
`.agents/skills/frontend-design-review/SKILL.md`

**For Angular-specific patterns**, see `fdf-angular-development.mdc`.

These skills are complementary:
- `frontend-design` → design creation and direction
- `frontend-design-review` → quality review and validation

## FDF UX Principles

FDF Management is an **operational system**. Every UI decision must optimize for:

1. **Operational speed** — users process records quickly under time pressure
2. **Clarity** — purpose of every screen is immediately obvious
3. **Low cognitive load** — minimise decisions, steps, and distractions
4. **Strong information hierarchy** — critical data is visually dominant
5. **Accessibility** — WCAG 2.1 AA minimum; usable by all staff
6. **Responsive/mobile usability** — critical for both portal and admin flows
7. **Design system consistency** — match existing Angular Material patterns already in use
8. **Clear validation and errors** — users understand what is wrong and how to fix it
9. **Safe destructive operations** — always confirm before delete/irreversible actions
10. **Role-aware interfaces** — show only what the current role requires

> Do not redesign something merely to make it visually different. Usability > aesthetics.

## Mandatory Scope

Apply these standards when creating or substantially modifying:
- Pages and route-level views
- Dialogs and overlays
- Forms (any form with more than one field)
- Navigation (sidebar, breadcrumbs, tabs)
- Tables and data grids
- Dashboards and summary views
- Cards and list items
- Mobile-specific layouts
- Any workflow requiring multiple sequential user actions

## Mobile-First / Responsive Requirements

All new UI must be usable on Desktop, Laptop, Tablet, and Mobile.

### Hard Requirements

- **No horizontal page scrolling** on any mobile viewport (320px minimum)
- **Touch targets ≥ 44×44px** for all interactive controls
- **Readable typography** — minimum 16px body text on mobile
- **Sensible form stacking** — single-column on mobile, multi-column where space allows
- **Responsive tables** — use horizontal scroll container, collapsible columns, or card fallback depending on data criticality; never silently truncate important data
- **Usable dialogs on small screens** — dialogs must not exceed viewport height; scrollable content inside dialog where necessary
- **Proper spacing** — minimum 8px between interactive elements on touch
- **Keyboard usability** — all interactive elements reachable via Tab; logical focus order
- **Visible focus states** — `:focus-visible` outlines present and clearly visible
- **Accessible form labels** — every input has an associated `<label>` or `aria-label`
- **Accessible error messages** — linked to input via `aria-describedby` or Angular Material error pattern
- **ARIA semantics** — use Angular Material semantics where available; add explicit ARIA only where Material does not already provide it
- **No information conveyed by color alone** — always pair color with icon, text, or pattern

## UI Completion Gate

Before declaring any UI work complete:
- [ ] `frontend-design-review` skill consulted
- [ ] Angular patterns correct (see `fdf-angular-development.mdc`)
- [ ] Desktop layout verified (≥1280px)
- [ ] Tablet layout verified (768px–1024px)
- [ ] Mobile layout verified (375px–767px)
- [ ] No horizontal scroll on 375px viewport
- [ ] Touch targets meet 44px minimum
- [ ] Keyboard navigation tested
- [ ] Focus indicators visible
- [ ] Form labels and error messages accessible
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA (4.5:1 text, 3:1 UI components)
- [ ] Loading state present for async operations
- [ ] Empty state handled gracefully
- [ ] Error state communicated clearly
- [ ] Destructive actions confirmed before execution
- [ ] Playwright E2E test updated (see `fdf-e2e-testing.mdc`)
- [ ] Security review performed where applicable (see `fdf-security.mdc`)
